# HAZARD for anything that shells out to `git check-ignore`: some blank-ish lines
# here make git report ANY path ending in "/" as ignored, so a bare "docs/nowhere/"
# reads back "ignored" whether or not anything ignores it -- a fail-open for a tool
# that treats "gitignored" as "absence is fine". The exact triggers are git-version-
# bound (a whitespace-only line and a lone CR from CRLF fire on git 2.53; a truly
# blank line does not), so the version-bound detail lives in one place rather than
# two: see tools/updater/README.md, "Asking git what is repository content", and
# issue #170. Do NOT delete the blank separators below to dodge this -- they are
# idiomatic; the fix is to never ask about a trailing-slash path, which the one
# consumer (tools/instruction_refs/check_instruction_references.py:is_git_ignored)
# already does, and any new consumer must too.
node_modules/
*.log

# Python (tools/updater)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.venv-*/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Drydock
.drydock/tmp/
# A dock's own working notes. `.github/copilot-instructions.md` describes a
# `DOCK.md` at the worktree root as the normal state of a dock, and routes
# assumptions and follow-ups into it, but nothing in the repository generates
# one. An agent that creates one for its own notes must not thereby commit it
# or redden the instruction-reference suite for every other checkout. See #395.
DOCK.md

# Local tooling
.claude/settings.local.json
.docks/

# Data refresh run state (evidence bundles, gate output, PR/issue bodies)
.modeltree-refresh/
